-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2024.1.5-2 (2026-11-17)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * ORDER 645: Debian's flightgear-data packages are no longer taken away. 2024.1.5-1 Conflicted with them, so apt removed
    them before it unpacked anything of ours, and Debian's flightgear-data-base removes its files through the link
    /usr/share/games/flightgear/Timezone -> ../../zoneinfo that its 1:2020.3.19 and older versions shipped and 1:2024.1.3
    replaced by a folder without dpkg-maintscript-helper symlink_to_dir: the link stayed, Debian's Timezone files were
    unpacked over tzdata's through it, and the removal deleted tzdata's files (Daniel's station, 2026-11-17: the clock fell to
    UTC). No script of this package can run before apt's removal (measured: apt removes first with Conflicts, with
    Conflicts and Replaces, and with a Pre-Depends), so the removal is gone: no Conflicts. When Debian's three data packages
    hold the recorded version the installer says so and downloads nothing (PRESENT_DEBIAN); data of another version is still
    refused with the message that names the files in the way.
  * A Timezone folder that is a link out of FlightGear's folder is never followed. The installer refuses to install through
    it (LINK) and keeps the problem "timezone-link" in sparky-stereo-problems, with the number of tzdata files missing or
    overwritten; Repair (flightgear-data-installer --repair-timezones) removes the link alone, reinstalls tzdata,
    tzdata-legacy and, if installed and still in the archive, flightgear-data-base, and reads the result back with
    dpkg --verify. The postrm and the installer remove a listed path only when the folder that holds it, every link
    followed, is still under the data folder.
  * Ten languages: the new sentences are in en, pl, pt_BR, fr, de, es, ja, ko, zh_CN and zh_TW (the problem's catalogs as well).
  * Depends: sparky-stereo-problems (>= 0.1.2).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2024.1.5-1 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * New (ORDER 399; Daniel, 2026-10-31: "we do not host it", "small downloader is better"): fetches FlightGear's 2024.1.5
    data release from its SourceForge release page, checks the recorded SHA-256, unpacks it in /usr/share/games/flightgear,
    Provides flightgear-data-all, -base, -ai and -models at 1:2024.1.5. Debian removed flightgear-data from testing on
    16 October (bug #1146394), so flightgear could not be installed.
  * Every failure (no network, a partial download, a hash that differs, no room, a file of another package in the way, a
    wrong version) stops and says what failed, why and what to do, in the nine languages; nothing half-unpacked is left.
